--- /dev/null
+++ b/.fabro/journal/01M1S5MWDTFSQBZ833Q74AGPXB.jsonl
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+{"$schema":"fabro-journal-v1","run_id":"01M1S5MWDTFSQBZ833Q74AGPXB","node":"planner","visit":1,"status":"succeeded","ts":"2026-09-05T16:22:10Z","data":{"painpoints":[{"text":"First `sd ready --limit 200` failed with exit 1: mise refused the untrusted config at `/repos/denkhaus/fabro/.mise.toml` (bun shim resolves through mise, so the bun-script `sd` CLI dies before running). Workaround: `mise trust /repos/denkhaus/fabro/.mise.toml`, then sd works. This burned several tool calls at session start; already tracked as seed fabro-66db (sandbox: pre-trust the repo mise config), so no new seed filed — but the painpoint reproduces in planner sessions too, not just implementer ones."}],"observations":["fabro-1e9f ('Diff evidence against the last seed boundary, not the run base') looks ALREADY IMPLEMENTED in the current tree: `evidence.nu` has `seed-claim-base` and `diff-section` anchored at the per-seed claim commit, exactly what its title describes — next planner should treat it as a verification-only candidate rather than fresh work.","Resolved a scope contradiction in fabro-4b57: the seed names only `evidence.nu`, but that script's header declares its output sections a contract with the reviewer prompt ('change wording there too'); the brief therefore includes the `reviewer.md` section-enumeration update to avoid reviewer ping-pong."]}}
